{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_<scrubbed>","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XiCciHMnbbEraXHcXs5TVp","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Codebase analysis for session token storage","subagent_type":"speckit-pro:codebase-analyst","prompt":"You are resolving a clarify question from the perspective of established codebase patterns and conventions.\n\nQUESTION (security-tagged):\nQ1: Should session tokens be stored in HttpOnly cookies or in localStorage with a 15-minute TTL?\n\nYOUR TASK:\nAnalyze the existing codebase to determine which approach aligns with established patterns. Look for:\n- Existing session/auth/token handling code (cookie config, localStorage usage, JWT handling, etc.)\n- Auth middleware, login/logout flows, refresh token mechanisms\n- CSRF protection (or lack of it) — relevant to cookie-based approaches\n- Frontend storage conventions already in use\n- Any prior security decisions encoded in code (e.g., `Secure`, `SameSite`, `HttpOnly` flags already set somewhere)\n- Framework conventions (e.g., Express session middleware, Next.js auth helpers, etc.)\n\nUse file_search, get_code_structure, Read, Glob, and Grep to gather evidence. Cite specific files and line numbers.\n\nReturn a structured answer:\n1. **Recommendation**: HttpOnly cookies OR localStorage+TTL OR \"no clear codebase signal\"\n2. **Evidence**: file paths and line numbers backing the recommendation\n3. **Confidence**: high / medium / low\n4. **Caveats**: any pattern conflicts or gaps you found\n\nDo NOT synthesize across other analysts' views. Do NOT write files. Return your structured answer only."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":"<scrubbed-usage>","diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<scrubbed-session>","uuid":"<scrubbed-uuid>"}
